# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Dimensions on screen at the view's scale (drawing quality plan, item 14).
# The 9 x 6 m box of facade_dimensions (300 mm outer walls, the south facade
# two walls in line, inner walls of 300 and 200 mm meeting it at x = 4 and
# 4.5), chained by 2461 and shown in a plan at 1:100. Its dimensions are
# recorded on paper (a canvas unit a millimetre) and on screen at 40 and
# 100 pixels to the metre, panned as well: a paper millimetre is then 4 and
# 10 pixels. On screen every size of a dimension is its paper size at the
# view's scale: the ticks, the extension lines' gap and overshoot, the
# value's lettering size and its place beside the line (the short steps'
# values moved past their segments too), so the screen recordings are the
# paper one magnified 4 and 10 times, their ratio the zoom's (2.5). The
# live plan keeps its layout (`record bim plan symbols of … keeping`) and
# only moves and magnifies it at another zoom, also when it was laid out
# zoomed far out (2 pixels to the metre, where the short steps span half a
# pixel), and lays it out again when the view's scale changes. Below 3
# pixels (8 pixels to the metre: 2 pixels) the values are left out and the
# lines stay, also when a layout made closer is shown there. At 1:20, 1:50
# and 1:200, at 200, 100 and 40 pixels to the metre, a paper millimetre is
# 4, 5 and 8 pixels, the screen the sheet at that scale magnified as many
# times.
import ui/panels/bim_plan_recording.dl

function check view scale {boolean:passed} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

# `amount` to hundredths, as "18.75".
function the view scale text of {a 64 bit floating-point number:amount}:
    execute:
        set hundredths to (the floor of (((the absolute value of amount) * 100.0) + 0.5)) as a 64 bit integer
        set sign to the string form of ""
        if (amount < 0.0) and (hundredths > (0 as a 64 bit integer)):
            set sign to the string form of "-"
        set fraction to the string form of (the remainder of hundredths divided by (100 as a 64 bit integer))
        if (the length of fraction) < 2:
            set fraction to (the string form of "0") + fraction
        return ((sign + (the string form of (hundredths / (100 as a 64 bit integer)))) + (the string form of ".")) + fraction

function the view scale transform centred at {cad vector2:centrePixel} on {cad vector2:modelSpot} at {a 64 bit floating-point number:pixelsPerMetre}:
    execute:
        return @intrinsic("construct", a bim drawing transform record, centrePixel, modelSpot, pixelsPerMetre)

# Where `screenPixel`, a pixel through `screenTransform`, stands on the
# paper of `paperTransform`.
function the view scale paper spot of {cad vector2:screenPixel} through {bim drawing transform record:screenTransform} on {bim drawing transform record:paperTransform}:
    execute:
        set modelX to screenTransform's origin's x + ((screenPixel's x - screenTransform's centre's x) / screenTransform's scale)
        set modelY to screenTransform's origin's y - ((screenPixel's y - screenTransform's centre's y) / screenTransform's scale)
        return the bim pixel of (a cad vector2 with x modelX and y modelY) through paperTransform

# The centrelines of the stroke quads of batch `batchIndex` of `canvas`, as
# pairs (`the bim stroke anchor of`).
function the view scale anchors of {bim canvas record:canvas} in batch {integer:batchIndex}:
    execute:
        set quadAnchors to an empty list of a cad vector2
        set corners to (the item at batchIndex in (canvas's batches's values))'s pixels's values
        set quadCount to (the length of corners) / 6
        loop quadCursor from 0 to quadCount:
            append (the bim stroke anchor of corners at (quadCursor * 6)) to quadAnchors
            append (the bim stroke anchor of corners at ((quadCursor * 6) + 2)) to quadAnchors
        return quadAnchors

# The lettering size of `label` on `canvas`, in its units: on paper the
# paper text height, on screen the drawing face as the replay scales its
# glyphs (`the bim replayed lettering scale of`).
function the view scale lettering size of {bim canvas text record:label} on {bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        if canvas's paperScale > 0.0:
            return (the bim lettering size of canvas) * (the bim lettering factor of label)
        return (the bim drawing face pixels) * (the bim replayed lettering scale of label at 1.0)

# How many labels of `canvas` have a height of their own: on screen the
# dimension values (the plan's other labels have none).
function the view scale value count on {bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        set found to 0
        loop labelCursor from 0 to the length of (canvas's texts's values):
            if (the item at labelCursor in (canvas's texts's values))'s height > 0.0:
                set found to found + 1
        return found

# The largest distance, in paper millimetres, between the stroke centrelines
# of batch `batchIndex` of `screen` (through `screenTransform`) brought onto
# paper and those of batch `paperBatch` of `paper`; 1000 when they differ in
# number.
function the view scale stroke offset of {bim canvas record:screenCanvas} batch {integer:batchIndex} through {bim drawing transform record:screenTransform} against {bim canvas record:paperCanvas} batch {integer:paperBatch} through {bim drawing transform record:paperTransform}:
    execute:
        set screenAnchors to the view scale anchors of screenCanvas in batch batchIndex
        set paperAnchors to the view scale anchors of paperCanvas in batch paperBatch
        set worst to 0.0
        if (the length of screenAnchors) != (the length of paperAnchors):
            set worst to 1000.0
        else:
            loop anchorCursor from 0 to the length of screenAnchors:
                set onPaper to the view scale paper spot of (the item at anchorCursor in screenAnchors) through screenTransform on paperTransform
                set worst to the maximum of worst and (the cad distance from onPaper to (the item at anchorCursor in paperAnchors))
        free screenAnchors
        free paperAnchors
        return worst

# The largest distance, in paper millimetres, between the values of
# `screen` from its label `firstScreen` on, brought onto paper, and those
# of `paper`, with their turn and lettering size (in paper millimetres) as
# the sheet's; 1000 when they differ in number, message or turn.
function the view scale value offset of {bim canvas record:screenCanvas} from {integer:firstScreen} through {bim drawing transform record:screenTransform} at {a 64 bit floating-point number:perMillimetre} against {bim canvas record:paperCanvas} through {bim drawing transform record:paperTransform}:
    execute:
        set worst to 0.0
        if ((the length of (screenCanvas's texts's values)) - firstScreen) != (the length of (paperCanvas's texts's values)):
            return 1000.0
        loop labelCursor from 0 to the length of (paperCanvas's texts's values):
            set paperLabel to the item at labelCursor in (paperCanvas's texts's values)
            set screenLabel to the item at (firstScreen + labelCursor) in (screenCanvas's texts's values)
            if (paperLabel's message != screenLabel's message) or ((the absolute value of (paperLabel's angle - screenLabel's angle)) > 1e-9):
                set worst to 1000.0
            set onPaper to the view scale paper spot of (a cad vector2 with x screenLabel's x and y screenLabel's y) through screenTransform on paperTransform
            set worst to the maximum of worst and (the cad distance from onPaper to (a cad vector2 with x paperLabel's x and y paperLabel's y))
            set sizeOff to ((the view scale lettering size of screenLabel on screenCanvas) / perMillimetre) - (the view scale lettering size of paperLabel on paperCanvas)
            set worst to the maximum of worst and (the absolute value of sizeOff)
        return worst

# The length of the first tick of `canvas` (its last batch), in its units.
function the view scale tick of {bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        set tickAnchors to the view scale anchors of canvas in batch ((the length of (canvas's batches's values)) - 1)
        set reach to the cad distance from (the item at 0 in tickAnchors) to (the item at 1 in tickAnchors)
        free tickAnchors
        return reach

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
begin bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
set layers to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "sand-lime", 0.3)) to layers
set outerType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Outer 300") with layers to target
free layers
set innerLayers to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "sand-lime", 0.2)) to innerLayers
set innerType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Inner 200") with innerLayers to target
free innerLayers
ignore add bim wall typed outerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 0.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed outerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 9.0 and y 0.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed outerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 9.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 9.0 and y 6.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed outerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 9.0 and y 6.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 6.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed outerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 6.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed outerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 6.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed innerType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 3.0) to target
set hundredView to add bim view of kind (bim plan view) named (the string form of "Plan 1:100") on editor's levelId to target
ignore set bim view hundredView scale to 100 and display to 0 in target
commit bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
type bim editor key 2461 in e
print editor's message as a line
set editor's planViewId to hundredView
set modelValue to editor's documentValue's current

# On paper at 1:100: a canvas unit a millimetre, the model origin at the
# paper origin.
set paperTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) at 10.0
set paperCanvas to a new bim canvas
set paperCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim dimensions in plan of editor through paperTransform on (the address of paperCanvas)

# On screen at 40 pixels to the metre (4 to the paper millimetre), and at
# 100 (10), centred elsewhere.
set nearTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 400.0 and y 300.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 3.0) at 40.0
set nearCanvas to a new bim canvas
draw bim dimensions in plan of editor through nearTransform on (the address of nearCanvas)
set closeTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 420.0 and y 310.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 2.5) at 100.0
set closeCanvas to a new bim canvas
draw bim dimensions in plan of editor through closeTransform on (the address of closeCanvas)

set paperTick to the view scale tick of paperCanvas
set nearTick to the view scale tick of nearCanvas
set closeTick to the view scale tick of closeCanvas
print ((the string form of "tick: ") + ((((the view scale text of paperTick) + (the string form of " mm on paper, ")) + ((the view scale text of nearTick) + (the string form of " px at 40 px/m, "))) + ((the view scale text of closeTick) + (the string form of " px at 100 px/m")))) as a line
check view scale (((the absolute value of (nearTick - (paperTick * 4.0))) < 1e-6) and ((the absolute value of (closeTick - (paperTick * 10.0))) < 1e-6)) named (the string form of "the tick is its paper size at the view's scale")
check view scale ((the absolute value of ((closeTick / nearTick) - 2.5)) < 1e-9) named (the string form of "the tick grows with the zoom")

set paperSize to the view scale lettering size of (the item at 0 in (paperCanvas's texts's values)) on paperCanvas
set nearSize to the view scale lettering size of (the item at 0 in (nearCanvas's texts's values)) on nearCanvas
set closeSize to the view scale lettering size of (the item at 0 in (closeCanvas's texts's values)) on closeCanvas
print ((the string form of "value lettered: ") + ((((the view scale text of paperSize) + (the string form of " mm on paper, ")) + ((the view scale text of nearSize) + (the string form of " px at 40 px/m, "))) + ((the view scale text of closeSize) + (the string form of " px at 100 px/m")))) as a line
check view scale ((the absolute value of ((closeSize / nearSize) - 2.5)) < 1e-9) named (the string form of "the value's lettering grows with the zoom")

set nearLines to the view scale stroke offset of nearCanvas batch 0 through nearTransform against paperCanvas batch 0 through paperTransform
set closeLines to the view scale stroke offset of closeCanvas batch 0 through closeTransform against paperCanvas batch 0 through paperTransform
set nearTicks to the view scale stroke offset of nearCanvas batch 1 through nearTransform against paperCanvas batch 1 through paperTransform
set closeTicks to the view scale stroke offset of closeCanvas batch 1 through closeTransform against paperCanvas batch 1 through paperTransform
check view scale ((((nearLines < 1e-6) and (closeLines < 1e-6)) and (nearTicks < 1e-6)) and (closeTicks < 1e-6)) named (the string form of "dimension and extension lines, leaders and ticks on screen are the paper's, magnified")
set nearValues to the view scale value offset of nearCanvas from 0 through nearTransform at 4.0 against paperCanvas through paperTransform
set closeValues to the view scale value offset of closeCanvas from 0 through closeTransform at 10.0 against paperCanvas through paperTransform
print ((the string form of "values off the paper's, in paper mm: ") + (((the view scale text of nearValues) + (the string form of " at 40 px/m, ")) + (the view scale text of closeValues))) as a line
check view scale ((nearValues < 1e-6) and (closeValues < 1e-6)) named (the string form of "every value stands where the sheet letters it, at its size, at both zooms")
print (the string form of "south values at 40 px/m (pixels), 100 px/m (pixels), paper (mm):") as a line
loop labelCursor from 0 to the length of (paperCanvas's texts's values):
    set paperLabel to the item at labelCursor in (paperCanvas's texts's values)
    if (paperLabel's y > 0.0) and (paperLabel's x < 90.0):
        set nearLabel to the item at labelCursor in (nearCanvas's texts's values)
        set closeLabel to the item at labelCursor in (closeCanvas's texts's values)
        set southRow to ((the string form of "  ") + paperLabel's message) + (the string form of " at ")
        set southRow to (southRow + (the view scale text of nearLabel's x)) + ((the string form of ", ") + (the view scale text of nearLabel's y))
        set southRow to (southRow + (the string form of "; ")) + (the view scale text of closeLabel's x)
        set southRow to (southRow + (the string form of ", ")) + (the view scale text of closeLabel's y)
        set southRow to (southRow + (the string form of "; ")) + (the view scale text of paperLabel's x)
        set southRow to (southRow + (the string form of ", ")) + (the view scale text of paperLabel's y)
        print southRow as a line

# The live plan: laid out once at 40 px/m, then moved and magnified to
# 100 px/m, as recorded there afresh.
set dimensionRecording to an empty bim dimension recording
set noPlaces to an empty list of a cad vector2
set liveNear to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through nearTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of dimensionRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan") on (the address of liveNear)
set liveClose to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through closeTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of dimensionRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan") on (the address of liveClose)
print ((the string form of "live plan layouts after a zoom: ") + (the string form of dimensionRecording's builds)) as a line
check view scale (dimensionRecording's builds = 1) named (the string form of "a zoom does not lay the dimensions out again")
set liveFirst to (the length of (liveClose's texts's values)) - (the length of (paperCanvas's texts's values))
set liveValues to the view scale value offset of liveClose from liveFirst through closeTransform at 10.0 against paperCanvas through paperTransform
set liveTicks to the view scale stroke offset of liveClose batch ((the length of (liveClose's batches's values)) - 1) through closeTransform against paperCanvas batch 1 through paperTransform
check view scale ((liveValues < 1e-6) and (liveTicks < 1e-6)) named (the string form of "the zoomed live plan matches the sheet's layout")
set liveAgain to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through closeTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of dimensionRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan changed") on (the address of liveAgain)
check view scale (dimensionRecording's builds = 2) named (the string form of "a changed plan lays them out again")

# Far out, at 8 px/m, a value's 2.5 mm is 2 pixels: the lines stay, the
# values are left out.
set farTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 400.0 and y 300.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 3.0) at 8.0
set farCanvas to a new bim canvas
draw bim dimensions in plan of editor through farTransform on (the address of farCanvas)
print ((the string form of "at 8 px/m: ") + (((the string form of (the length of (farCanvas's texts's values))) + (the string form of " values, ")) + ((the string form of (the length of (farCanvas's batches's values))) + (the string form of " stroke batches")))) as a line
check view scale (((the length of (farCanvas's texts's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (farCanvas's batches's values)) = 2)) named (the string form of "values below 3 pixels are left out, the lines stay")

# Laid out on the live plan at 40 px/m and shown at 8: the values are left
# out there as well, the lines stay.
set fadedRecording to an empty bim dimension recording
set liveLaid to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through nearTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of fadedRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan") on (the address of liveLaid)
set liveFar to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through farTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of fadedRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan") on (the address of liveFar)
print ((the string form of "live plan at 40 then 8 px/m: ") + ((((the string form of (the view scale value count on liveLaid)) + (the string form of " and ")) + ((the string form of (the view scale value count on liveFar)) + (the string form of " values, "))) + (((the string form of (the length of (liveLaid's batches's values))) + (the string form of " and ")) + ((the string form of (the length of (liveFar's batches's values))) + (the string form of " stroke batches"))))) as a line
check view scale (((fadedRecording's builds = 1) and ((the view scale value count on liveLaid) = (the length of (paperCanvas's texts's values)))) and (((the view scale value count on liveFar) = 0) and ((the length of (liveFar's batches's values)) = (the length of (liveLaid's batches's values))))) named (the string form of "the kept layout zoomed out leaves its values out, its lines stay")

# Laid out zoomed far out, at 2 px/m (the 250 and the 200 spanning half a
# pixel and less), and shown at 100: the sheet's layout all the same, every
# tick in place.
set tinyTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 400.0 and y 300.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 3.0) at 2.0
set tinyRecording to an empty bim dimension recording
set liveTiny to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through tinyTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of tinyRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan") on (the address of liveTiny)
set liveGrown to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through closeTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of tinyRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan") on (the address of liveGrown)
set grownFirst to (the length of (liveGrown's texts's values)) - (the length of (paperCanvas's texts's values))
set grownValues to the view scale value offset of liveGrown from grownFirst through closeTransform at 10.0 against paperCanvas through paperTransform
set grownBatches to the length of (liveGrown's batches's values)
set grownLines to the view scale stroke offset of liveGrown batch (grownBatches - 2) through closeTransform against paperCanvas batch 0 through paperTransform
set grownTicks to the view scale stroke offset of liveGrown batch (grownBatches - 1) through closeTransform against paperCanvas batch 1 through paperTransform
print ((the string form of "laid out at 2 px/m, shown at 100: off the sheet by ") + (((the view scale text of grownValues) + (the string form of " mm (values), ")) + (((the view scale text of grownLines) + (the string form of " (lines), ")) + ((the view scale text of grownTicks) + (the string form of " (ticks)"))))) as a line
check view scale (((tinyRecording's builds = 1) and (grownValues < 1e-6)) and ((grownLines < 1e-6) and (grownTicks < 1e-6))) named (the string form of "a layout made zoomed far out holds magnified")

# Other view scales: the paper millimetre on screen follows the view's
# denominator as well as the zoom.
set denominators to an empty list of an integer
append 20 to denominators
append 50 to denominators
append 200 to denominators
set zooms to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
append 200.0 to zooms
append 100.0 to zooms
append 40.0 to zooms
set millimetres to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
append 4.0 to millimetres
append 5.0 to millimetres
append 8.0 to millimetres
loop scaleCursor from 0 to the length of denominators:
    set denominator to the item at scaleCursor in denominators
    set zoomScale to the item at scaleCursor in zooms
    set perMillimetre to the item at scaleCursor in millimetres
    begin bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
    ignore set bim view hundredView scale to denominator and display to 0 in (the address of (editor's documentValue's current))
    commit bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
    set scaledPaperTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) at (1000.0 / (denominator as a 64 bit floating-point number))
    set scaledPaper to a new bim canvas
    set scaledPaper's paperScale to 1.0
    draw bim dimensions in plan of editor through scaledPaperTransform on (the address of scaledPaper)
    set scaledTransform to the view scale transform centred at (a cad vector2 with x 410.0 and y 290.0) on (a cad vector2 with x 4.2 and y 2.8) at zoomScale
    set scaledScreen to a new bim canvas
    draw bim dimensions in plan of editor through scaledTransform on (the address of scaledScreen)
    set scaledTick to (the view scale tick of scaledScreen) / (the view scale tick of scaledPaper)
    set scaledLetters to (the view scale lettering size of (the item at 0 in (scaledScreen's texts's values)) on scaledScreen) / (the view scale lettering size of (the item at 0 in (scaledPaper's texts's values)) on scaledPaper)
    set scaledLines to the view scale stroke offset of scaledScreen batch 0 through scaledTransform against scaledPaper batch 0 through scaledPaperTransform
    set scaledTicks to the view scale stroke offset of scaledScreen batch 1 through scaledTransform against scaledPaper batch 1 through scaledPaperTransform
    set scaledValues to the view scale value offset of scaledScreen from 0 through scaledTransform at perMillimetre against scaledPaper through scaledPaperTransform
    print ((((the string form of "1:") + (the string form of denominator)) + ((the string form of " at ") + (the view scale text of zoomScale))) + (((the string form of " px/m: tick and lettering x") + (the view scale text of scaledTick)) + ((the string form of " and x") + (the view scale text of scaledLetters)))) as a line
    set scaledName to ((the string form of "at 1:") + (the string form of denominator)) + (the string form of " the screen is the sheet magnified by its paper millimetre")
    check view scale ((((the absolute value of (scaledTick - perMillimetre)) < 1e-6) and ((the absolute value of (scaledLetters - perMillimetre)) < 1e-6)) and (((scaledLines < 1e-6) and (scaledTicks < 1e-6)) and (scaledValues < 1e-6))) named scaledName

# The live plan's kept layout follows the view's scale: at 1:200 now, under
# the same plan key, it is laid out again.
set liveRescaled to a new bim canvas
record bim plan symbols of editor placing labels at noPlaces through closeTransform lettered at 13.0 keeping (the address of dimensionRecording) keyed (the string form of "plan changed") on (the address of liveRescaled)
check view scale (dimensionRecording's builds = 3) named (the string form of "a changed view scale lays them out again")
free denominators
free zooms
free millimetres
free noPlaces
